{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012UVpuQn7MTSPSrUSGnN5jV","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer:\\\\n\\\\n**The storage formatting tool writes `meta.properties V1` when using the --cluster-id flag.**\\\\n\\\\nThis is documented in **`/store/prs/21547-kafka-20176-metaproperties-v2.md`**, which states:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"This PR will not actually write `meta.properties V2` anywhere. Formatting will still write `meta.properties V1` to enforce that cluster.id is always present.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis is in the context of the proposal for brokers and observer controllers to skip storage formatting (KIP-1262). While the proposal introduces a V2 format to support optional cluster.id, the actual storage formatting tool continues to write **V1** to ensure that the cluster.id field is always present when formatting occurs (such as during bootstrap controller initialization with the --cluster-id flag).\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"issues/kafka-20208-update-meta-properties-clusteridrecord.md\\\",\\\"prs/21547-kafka-20176-metaproperties-v2.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1262-auto-formatting-directories.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1262-auto-formatting.md\\\",\\\"issues/kafka-20176-metaproperties-v2.md\\\",\\\"WINDOW-82-SUMMARY.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":36.08,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":217656,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":15554,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.06737760000000001,\\\"input_tokens\\\":114,\\\"output_tokens\\\":2878}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"479795fc-bcb0-4120-b225-656b5a7a1c6d","uuid":"e8341712-9ca2-4c28-aeb0-f6fd7cd1fe1a","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:19:29.580Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer:\\\\n\\\\n**The storage formatting tool writes `meta.properties V1` when using the --